  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There are at least three locations in the code where ObjectProfile objects are serialized into XML:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "fedora.server.access.FedoraAccessServlet",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "fedora.server.access.defaultdisseminator.ObjectInfoAsXML",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "fedora.server.rest.DefaultSerializer",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Other API-A and API-M result objects are similarly serialized to XML in multiple locations. There are also two XML representations for method listings and datastream listings. Method listing XML conforms to either listMethods.xsd or objectMethods.xsd. Datastream listing XML conforms to either listDatastreams.xsd or objectItemIndex.xsd.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Each API-A/M response object should have a single schema and should be serialized in one place in the code. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
